cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below and also credit the original sources listed in docs/SOURCES.md."
type: dataset
title: "AyurKB: a bilingual, hybrid Ayurveda knowledge base for expert systems"
abstract: >-
  AyurKB links Ayurvedic diagnosis, materia medica, remedies and modern scientific evidence in one relational
  dataset with English, Hindi and Sanskrit representations. It integrates authoritative, openly licensed and
  permission-sensitive sources, including NAMASTE, WHO, USDA, GBIF, Wikidata, NLM, PubChem, Europe PMC
  and a community herb database. It includes metadata and extracted observations from 565 published case
  reports and internal computational benchmarks. Source permissions, semantic and language adjudication,
  and independent clinical validation remain incomplete.
